  "Question": "In a Cartesian coordinate plane, circle \\(C\\) has center \\((3,4)\\) and radius 4. The relative positions of circle \\(C\\) with respect to the \\(x\\)-axis and the \\(y\\)-axis, respectively, are",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Tangent; tangent",
    "B": "Tangent; intersecting at 2 points",
    "C": "Intersecting at 2 points; tangent",
    "D": "Disjoint; intersecting at 2 points"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The distance from the center to the \\(x\\)-axis is \\(4=r\\), so they are tangent. The distance to the \\(y\\)-axis is \\(3<4\\), so they intersect.",
